Touro College of Dental Medicine (TCDM), the first pre-doctoral dental program based in New Mexico, celebrated the official grand opening of its dental clinical training facility on the Lovelace Biomedical Research Institute (LBRI) campus in Albuquerque, N.M. The new 70,000 square foot facility houses more than 100 dental units accommodating students who will be completing their education and clinical training in New Mexico.
